  "body": "Closes #170\nClaim: mac/m4-captures\n\n**Problem.** LOT-100 (#191) needed the new-topic form's poll section. `R45a` (`nouveau_sujet.htm`) has none.\n\n**What was captured.** One read-only GET as user1, 2026-11-10 (`R170a`), of the separate new-poll form `/hfr/<cat>/nouveau_sondage.htm` that the topic lists link (`#md_btn_new_poll`, `R04`):\n- It is the `R45a` form with a hidden `sond=1` and the `div#sondagediv` block: `textreponse0` (the question), `textreponse1`-`10` (answers, `maxlength` 255), `allowvisitor`, `max_votes` 1-10, and the closing date `jour`/`mois`/`annee`/`heure`/`minute`.\n- Neither new-topic form has a `have_sondage` input; the first-post edit form `R63b` has one.\n- Legacy's \"form allows a poll\" test requires that input (`HFRswift/Swift/ReplyService.swift:279-281` @ `87fe0d1c`), so legacy never offers a poll on either new-topic form.\n\n**What changed.**\n- `R170a` and its meta, `corpus.json`, a `MANIFEST.md` row.\n- HFR-PROTOCOL §6b: a \"New poll\" bullet.\n- LOT-100 spec: the fixture pointers; the #170 pending marks are removed.\n\n**Not captured.** What `bddpost.php` answers to a poll post (a public write).\n\n**Leak check.** An independent Sonnet sub-agent, separate from the redactor, found 0 hits for pseudos, credentials, cookies, `hash_check` and e-mail addresses. `check --corpus` and `check --config` are clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CJ1auuPWv2FeT7Q4Ps\n",
